1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,070
Listen to a talk on an art podcast.

2
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:13,210
Today, we'll dive into the world of cubism, an innovative art movement that revolutionized the way we perceive and represent reality.

3
00:00:13,210 --> 00:00:21,070
Cubism emerged in the early 20th century, spearheaded by artists like Pablo Picasso and Georges Braque.

4
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:23,203
Unlike traditional art,

5
00:00:23,203 --> 00:00:26,180
which aimed to depict subjects from a single viewpoint

6
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:32,259
cubism fragmented objects into geometric shapes and presented multiple angles simultaneously.

7
00:00:32,259 --> 00:00:37,901
This technique challenged conventional perspectives and provided a more dynamic

8
00:00:37,901 --> 00:00:40,290
and complex representation of the subject matter.

9
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:47,602
One of the most iconic works of cubism is Picasso's painting "Les Demoiselles d'Avignon,"

10
00:00:47,602 --> 00:00:49,290
or "The Young Ladies of Avignon" in English.

11
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:57,040
It was revolutionary, breaking away from realism with distorted figures and jagged geometric shapes.

12
00:00:57,040 --> 00:01:02,060
It rejected the traditional perspective, presenting multiple viewpoints at once.

13
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:06,250
And the painting shocked audiences with its raw, fragmented forms.

14
00:01:06,250 --> 00:01:09,466
Cubism can be divided into two phases:

15
00:01:09,466 --> 00:01:12,240
Analytical Cubism and Synthetic Cubism.

16
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:19,240
Analytical Cubism focused on deconstructing objects into basic geometric forms and muted colors

17
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:26,533
while Synthetic Cubism introduced brighter colors and collage techniques, integrating different materials like newspapers

18
00:01:26,533 --> 00:01:28,180
and fabric into the artwork.

19
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:36,000
The impact of cubism extended beyond the visual arts, influencing literature, architecture and even music.

20
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,140
Its emphasis on abstraction and multiplicity of perspectives inspired artists

21
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:46,100
and thinkers to explore new ways of expressing ideas and interpreting the world.

22
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:53,200
Ultimately, cubism paved the way for many modern art movements, leaving a lasting legacy on artistic expression.
